<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<model>
    <name>kitchen_base_cabinets</name>
    <version>1.0</version>
    <sdf version='1.6'>model.sdf</sdf>
    <author>
        <name>Ilia O.</name>
        <email>iliao@kaia.ai</email>
    </author>
    <description>A 2.35 m run of kitchen base units with an integrated
    stainless sink and faucet, at true residential dimensions: 0.900 m counter
    height, 0.635 m counter depth, 0.600 m carcass, and a 0.089 m high by
    0.076 m deep toe kick (3.5" x 3", US standard). The toe kick is
    deliberately lower than the 0.097 m robot, so the robot cannot enter it -
    that is the case the extendable side brush and mop exist for.

    Authored rather than reused because Fuel has no suitable asset:
    KitchenCountertop is a CHART lab bench with its surface at 0.74 m, no toe
    kick, and a cooktop welded into a single-object mesh AND painted into its
    diffuse texture; KitchenSink is a floor-standing unit with its counter at
    0.75 m and likewise no toe kick.

    Origin is at the back (wall) face, centred along the length, on the floor;
    the run grows towards -y, so place it at the wall plane with yaw 0.

    Textures are reused from models already vendored in this package:
    wood.png from Cabinet, marble.png from TableMarble.</description>
</model>
